## What we build

Console TODO list. Assembles: arrays, structs, functions, strings, files.

## Model

```c
typedef struct {
    char text[100];
    int done;
} Task;
```

`done` = 0/1 — not done/done.

## Functions

```c
#define MAX 100

int addTask(Task tasks[], int count, const char *text);
void showTasks(Task tasks[], int count);
void markDone(Task tasks[], int count, int index);
int saveTasks(const char *file, Task tasks[], int count);
int loadTasks(const char *file, Task tasks[]);
```

- `addTask` — copy into `tasks[count]`, return `count + 1`
- `showTasks` — `for`, output `[x]` or `[ ]`
- `markDone` — `tasks[index].done = 1`
- `saveTasks` — open file, `fprintf` in loop, return count
- `loadTasks` — open, `fgets` in loop, return count

## Example: saveTasks

```c
int saveTasks(const char *file, Task tasks[], int count) {
    FILE *f = fopen(file, "w");
    if (f == NULL) return -1;
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        fprintf(f, "%d %s\n", tasks[i].done, tasks[i].text);
    }
    fclose(f);
    return count;
}
```

## Example: showTasks

```c
void showTasks(Task tasks[], int count) {
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        printf("%d. [%c] %s\n", i + 1, tasks[i].done ? 'x' : ' ', tasks[i].text);
    }
}
```

## What if

- Array too small — check `count < MAX`.
- `strcpy` into small buffer — overflow.

## Summary

- struct + array + functions
- Files — save/load
- Checks on `NULL`, `count`
- Ternary — for status

