## Putting it all together

The course covered: types, loops, functions, arrays, strings, pointers, memory, structs, files.

## Model

```c
typedef struct {
    char name[30];
    int age;
} Person;
```

Array of several `Person` + functions.

## Final example

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

typedef struct {
    char name[30];
    int age;
} Person;

Person oldest(Person arr[], int n) {
    Person result = arr[0];
    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
        if (arr[i].age > result.age) result = arr[i];
    }
    return result;
}

int main(void) {
    Person people[] = {{"Ivan", 25}, {"Maria", 30}, {"Peter", 28}};
    Person o = oldest(people, 3);
    printf("Oldest: %s (%d)\n", o.name, o.age);
    return 0;
}
```

## Checks

- Struct with fields
- Array of structs
- Function with array
- Return struct or pointer
- `printf` with `%s` and `%d`

## What if

- Forget `strcpy` — error.
- `sizeof` in a function — pointer size.
- `free` after `malloc` — mandatory.

## Summary

- Combine structs + arrays + functions
- Check string lengths
- Return structs by value (copy) or pointer
- `printf` with correct specifiers

